     1	//! Config storage helpers backed by sea-orm.
     2	//!
     3	//! Two APIs exist side-by-side:
     4	//!
     5	//! 1. [`ConfigKv`] (preferred) — flat dotted keys like `remote.origin.url` stored
     6	//!    in the `config_kv` table, with per-row encryption support and a richer
     7	//!    set of CRUD primitives (`set`, `add`, `unset`, `unset_all`, regex/prefix
     8	//!    queries). All new code should use this API.
     9	//! 2. [`Config`] (deprecated) — three-column form `(configuration, name, key)`
    10	//!    stored in the legacy `config` table. Retained for backwards-compatible
    11	//!    repos that have not yet migrated.
    12	//!
    13	//! Both APIs follow the same `*_with_conn` transaction-safety convention used
    14	//! by [`crate::internal::branch`]: callers inside an open transaction must use
    15	//! the `_with_conn` variants to avoid acquiring a second pool connection
    16	//! (which deadlocks under SQLite's writer-serialisation).
    17	//!
    18	//! Cross-cutting helpers in this module:
    19	//! - [`resolve_env`] / [`resolve_env_for_target`]: cascading env-var resolution
    20	//!   (process env > local repo config > global config).
    21	//! - [`is_sensitive_key`] / [`is_vault_internal_key`]: heuristics that drive the
    22	//!   encrypt-by-default policy in `libra config`.
    23	//! - [`encrypt_value`] / [`decrypt_value`]: thin wrappers over the vault module.
